    "body": "## Current scope and result\n\nMora authorized implementation on 2026-10-05; the adopted design and subsequent findings are recorded in [DECISIONS.md](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/blob/claude/pensive-meitner-wrg9b0/nix/sandhi/docs/DECISIONS.md).\n\nStage A now demonstrates direct transport between two separately configured Sandhi installations: mutual TLS, certificate-to-installation mapping, bounded messages, durable inbox/outbox state, restart recovery, a replaceable deterministic responder, Nix packaging, and a three-guest NixOS experiment. No GitHub relay or human message forwarding is used during the measured exchange.\n\n## Evidence and validation\n\n- **VM attempt 4 on a990b99:** all eleven acceptance assertions passed; 793.5 seconds of test script under software emulation, no harness errors. Both existing CI workflows succeeded on that exact source.\n- **Independent artifact reading, 45813be:** 15 endpoint archives and 18 successful message pairs checked; split-input digests recomputed; acknowledgments, parent chains, endpoint outcomes, and journal restarts cross-checked. This is an offline reading, not a second VM execution.\n- **65 portable Python tests passed**, including real TLS/process exchanges, recovery regressions, and six evidence-corruption tests.\n- Three original public certificates and both installation maps were recovered from the existing driver log and independently verified. The untrusted probe's public certificate was not retained; its recorded fingerprint and observed TLS refusal remain. This gap is explicit.\n- Attempts 1–3 remain recorded with their sources and failures. Production modules, `flake.nix` and `realize.py` are unchanged.\n- The later certificate-export fix in d48a439 applies to future runs; attempt 4 does not validate that later experiment revision.\n\nReproduce the offline review from the repository root:\n\n```sh\npython3 nix/sandhi/scripts/check_exchange_evidence.py \\\n  nix/sandhi/evidence/stage-a-2026-10-05/attempt-4 \\\n  --expected-source a990b9983166598ed6fd3e3c92414c231667173b\n```\n\nRecords: [attempt 4](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/tree/claude/pensive-meitner-wrg9b0/nix/sandhi/evidence/stage-a-2026-10-05/attempt-4), [Tessera's derived reviews](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/tree/claude/pensive-meitner-wrg9b0/nix/sandhi/evidence/stage-a-2026-10-05/tessera-review), and [review handoff](https://github.com/mora-vector/strange-anchor/pull/6#issuecomment-5999047429).\n\n## Limits and next gate\n\nResponders are deterministic. This establishes transport, not an exchange between AI model families. Both installations used one builder/operator. The network claim covers the observed contract restrictions and removed default route; the QEMU host-facing link remained. Peer withdrawal restarted the service, so uninterrupted-connection behavior was not measured.\n\nStage B needs a concrete model/adapter scope, artifact identities and licenses, resource/download bounds, and model-input/output evidence before model execution. Hosted credentials or spending are not enabled by this PR.\n\n## Original proposal description (historical)\n\nThe text below predates Mora's authorization and the implementation. Its docs-only status is superseded by the current status above.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Sideband's original proposal description</summary>\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds `nix/sandhi/docs/PROPOSAL-STANDALONE-EXCHANGE.md`, a discussion document for the question: can two independently installed copies of Sandhi carry a conversation between AI agents from different model families, with no GitHub dependency and no person relaying messages?\n\n- Records the shared finding (Tessera and this Claude session): the current package has no communication endpoint, model adapter, peer authentication, conversation state or message-evidence integration.\n- Lists constraints read from the code that shape a design: ingress filtering, no low ports, finite `runtimeMaxSec`, public contract values, IPv4 literals, and the experiment-0 DNS path.\n- Proposes four stages: (A) deterministic transport, (B) local open-weight models, (C) hosted adapters, which need Mora's decision, and (D) separate operators.\n- Ends with open questions for Tessera and Mora.\n\nThis PR is the thread for that dialogue. It is not a decision; accepted scope goes into DECISIONS.md before any code. No modules, tests, workflows or archive objects change.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `python3 anchor.py verify` passes. Docs-only, so the Sandhi workflow is not triggered by design.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu)_\n\n</details>\n",
